WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.680
A cochlear implant bypasses damaged hair cells and stimulates surviving auditory

2
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.200
neurons. It gives many adults with severe hearing loss useful hearing.

3
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:18.600
That is the clinical payoff: electrical stimulation can support speech

4
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.640
understanding. The implant borrows the cochlea's frequency map.

5
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.660
Higher frequencies go to basal contacts, lower ones to apical contacts.

6
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.140
Which neurons get which information?

7
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.400
That question runs through sensory prostheses.

8
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:35.930
A contact is hardware.

9
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.250
A channel is a band of frequency information.

10
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.250
Neighbouring contacts produce overlapping electric fields, called channel

11
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.910
interaction. So more contacts do not mean as many independent channels.

12
00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:54.710
Useful sensation depends on which surviving neurons receive the signal and the

13
00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.710
pattern it carries.

14
00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:58.730
Electrode count alone cannot tell us that.

15
00:00:59.633 --> 00:01:02.393
In the retina, targeting shapes what people see.

16
00:01:03.173 --> 00:01:08.453
An electrode on the inner surface sits beside ganglion-cell axons passing toward the

17
00:01:08.453 --> 00:01:14.213
optic disk. Implant users often drew elongated or distorted shapes from single

18
00:01:14.213 --> 00:01:18.273
electrodes. An axon-pathway model accounted for those shapes.

19
00:01:19.113 --> 00:01:22.753
This is a model-supported explanation, not a direct recording.

20
00:01:23.653 --> 00:01:25.673
One electrode does not make one pixel.

21
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:31.057
Retinal implants can provide limited vision after photoreceptor loss.

22
00:01:31.977 --> 00:01:37.457
In the PRIMA design, pixels beneath the retina turn projected near-infrared light

23
00:01:37.457 --> 00:01:40.037
into current that stimulates bipolar cells.

24
00:01:40.857 --> 00:01:44.137
The signal then passes through the remaining retinal network.

25
00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:49.297
Early participants with optimal chip placement achieved prosthetic acuity.

26
00:01:50.277 --> 00:01:54.477
Later trial benefits came with serious device- or procedure-related events.

27
00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.910
Optogenetics changes the surviving cells.

28
00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.970
A viral vector makes them express a light-sensitive protein.

29
00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:08.190
In one adult with retinitis pigmentosa, treated ganglion cells responded to light

30
00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.410
from engineered goggles.

31
00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:14.690
With the treated eye and goggles, the patient located, counted and touched objects.

32
00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.370
Without the goggles, the patient did not detect objects.

33
00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:23.670
This was partial, goggle-dependent function in one person, not normal vision.

34
00:02:24.733 --> 00:02:28.653
Touch can be written into a peripheral nerve or into sensory cortex.

35
00:02:29.813 --> 00:02:34.453
Nerve stimulation produced phantom-hand touch in people with amputations and helped

36
00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:36.013
them handle delicate objects.

37
00:02:36.873 --> 00:02:42.153
In one man with a spinal cord injury, motor-cortex signals controlled a robotic arm.

38
00:02:43.053 --> 00:02:47.553
Stimulation of sensory cortex supplied touch feedback and shortened his task time.

39
00:02:48.273 --> 00:02:51.793
That supports feedback for this person, not a population effect.

40
00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:57.577
The design rule is to reproduce task-relevant features of the natural neural code,

41
00:02:57.937 --> 00:02:59.777
then test perception and behaviour.

42
00:03:00.917 --> 00:03:03.137
Biomimicry is an evidence-backed strategy.

43
00:03:04.037 --> 00:03:08.217
It is not a proven law that more exact copying always improves performance.
